// Local-dev override — copy to go.work (gitignored) to edit the kernel in place.
//
//	cp go.work.example go.work
//
// go.mod stays authoritative: it pins github.com/dreplyai/go-assistant-core to a
// released tag, which is what CI and any fresh clone build from. This file swaps
// that for the sibling checkout so a change in the kernel is picked up without a
// tag-and-bump round trip.
//
// Do NOT commit go.work, and do not reintroduce a `replace` in go.mod to get the
// same effect. A replace is invisible to whoever clones the repo next: it makes
// the build pass on the one machine that has the sibling directory and fail
// everywhere else. That is exactly how this dependency spent its first months —
// buildable only here, because the repo it named did not exist yet.
//
// Before pushing, verify the build BOTH ways: with go.work present, and with it
// moved aside. Only the second one proves the pin is real.
//
// Known gap while go-modules is in the use block: `go build` passes without
// this file, `go test` does not — corpus_pair_test.go needs
// search.SetCurrentForTest, which is unreleased. Closes when go-modules is
// tagged and the pin bumped.

go 1.25.0

use (
	.
	../go-assistant-core
	// go-modules is here too while corpus/ needs search changes that are not
	// tagged yet — currently SetCurrentForTest, without which nothing that
	// retrieves can be tested outside a live Qdrant. Remove once released.
	../redelay/go-modules
)
